[[2047,16,8,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The radio \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied directly\n(pins 4 and 7 of connector A) by the battery via the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              and the maxifuse J/B1 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>It receives a supply when the ignition is\nswitched on (INT) (pin 3 of connector A) via the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>With the side lights switched on, the supply\nreaches pin 6 of connector A by means of the line coming from the\nswitch for the steering column switch unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; the radio\ncontrols are therefore lit up when the side lights are switched\non.</p><p>Pin 8 of connector A, on the other hand,\nis earthed (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>Pin 5 of connector A is connected to the\ncontrol unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P22</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which controls the aerial built into the\nheated rear windscreen. The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P22</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is then connected\nto the radio by means of the specific aerial lead.</p><p>Connector B sends out cables carrying signals to the speakers:</p><ul><li>pins 5 and 6 to left front loudspeakers <strong>P35</strong> and <strong>P45</strong> ,</li><li>pins 3 and 4 to the right front loudspeakers <strong>P36</strong> and <strong>P46</strong> ,</li><li>pins 7 and 8 to the left rear speakers <strong>P30</strong> and <strong>P40</strong> ,</li><li>pins 1 and 2 to the right rear speakers <strong>P31</strong> and <strong>P41</strong> .</li></ul>"]]